    <!-- ─── Privacy ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="np" id="privacy">
      <div class="container np__inner reveal">
        <div class="np__copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Privacy · honest version</span>
          <h2>Your notes never leave your device.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Pulse stores everything in a local SQLite database on your Android
            device. The full-text search index is the same database. The recall
            step is the same local model that runs chat. Nothing crosses the
            network boundary.
          </p>
          <ul class="np__list" role="list">
            <li>
              <strong>Local only, forever:</strong> no accounts, no signup, no
              cloud. Wipe the app's data folder and you get a clean install.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Free sync, today:</strong> the <code>notes.db</code> file is
              plain SQLite. Drop the app data folder into a git repo, a Syncthing
              pair, or a folder-sync tool and you have manual sync without paying
              anyone.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Pro sync, planned for v0.7:</strong> opt-in
              end-to-end-encrypted sync across devices. Pro is the only path that
              uses the network. Disable it and nothing changes.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="np__more">
            Full audit, source code, and the security model live on the
            <a href="/privacy/">Security &amp; privacy</a> page.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="np__card glass" aria-label="What Pulse does and does not do">
          <h3 class="np__card-title">What Pulse does.</h3>
          <ul class="np__card-list np__card-list--yes" role="list">
            <li>Stores notes in a local SQLite database on the device</li>
            <li>Runs FTS5 search on the same database</li>
            <li>Calls the local model over loopback</li>
            <li>Surfaces relevant notes from the local index</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="np__card-title">What Pulse does not do.</h3>
          <ul class="np__card-list np__card-list--no" role="list">
            <li>Send your notes anywhere by default</li>
            <li>Read SMS, notifications, or other apps</li>
            <li>Phone home with usage telemetry</li>
            <li>Train a model on your data, ever</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

